# L2-1767: the Micheline binary decoder must not overflow the native stack on
# deeply-nested input reached through UNPACK.
# https://linear.app/tezos/issue/L2-1767  (fix: tezos/tezos!22367)
#
# `input` and `code` below are the issue's attached repro (unpack_stack_overflow.tzt)
# verbatim. The DUP;CONCAT loop doubles `0x0500` k=24 times, giving 2^24 copies of
# `05 00`; with the PACK tag `0x05` and an `Int 0` leaf (`00 00`) that is the packed
# form of a 2^24 = 16,777,216-deep chain of single-argument primitives. The payload
# is built at runtime, so this file stays tiny and the 32 KB operation-size limit
# is irrelevant -- that is the point of the shape.
#
#   WITHOUT the decode-depth bound: the decoder recurses ~16.7M levels and the
#   process dies with `Fatal error: exception Stack overflow`.
#   WITH the bound: the decode is rejected, and the post-decode `unpack_failed`
#   penalty then exhausts the operation gas -- hence `output Gas_exhaustion`.
#
# NB the issue's repro has `output { }`: it was written to be run against an
# UNBOUNDED decoder, where the process aborts and no output is produced. Against
# the bounded decoder the run terminates in Gas_exhaustion, so the expectation is
# adjusted here; everything else is unchanged.
#
# k=24 is chosen because the crash window is bounded on both sides and slides with
# the stack size (see the issue):
#   - k=25 (67 MB) exhausts gas on UNPACK's saturating 20*len gate BEFORE decoding;
#   - k<=23 decodes successfully below the stack threshold on a 12.5 MB stack and
#     dies in the unpack_failed penalty instead;
#   - a stack of ~20 MB or more survives k=24 entirely (the issue's operational
#     stopgap), so on such a machine this test passes even against an unbounded
#     decoder. If the CI stack size changes, re-verify against an unfixed build.
#
# NB this test is excluded from the file list handed to MIR's tzt_runner (see
# etherlink/ci/etherlink_ci.ml): MIR still decodes Micheline recursively and
# does not meter decoding gas, so it aborts on this input rather than reporting
# a result. Only the octez-client TZT runner exercises it here.
input { Stack_elt int 24 };
output Gas_exhaustion;
code { PUSH bytes 0x0500 ; SWAP ; PUSH bool True ;
       LOOP { DIG 1 ; DUP ; CONCAT ; DUG 1 ; PUSH int -1 ; ADD ; DUP ; GT };
       DROP ; PUSH bytes 0x0000 ; SWAP ; CONCAT ; PUSH bytes 0x05 ; CONCAT ;
       UNPACK nat ; DROP ; } ;
